WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:02.972
Bitcoin mines hashes.

2
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:05.880
Hashes that nobody will ever read.

3
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:07.885
So you keep proof of work...

4
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:09.600
...and change the work.

5
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.000
Every block becomes a matrix product,

6
00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:15.131
computed on the GPUs miners already own.

7
00:00:16.339 --> 00:00:18.398
Vearl mines AI.

8
00:00:18.789 --> 00:00:22.456
Miners run AI models, for real clients.

9
00:00:22.639 --> 00:00:25.639
Every answer is checked before anyone gets paid.

10
00:00:25.689 --> 00:00:28.639
One wrong number, and the cheater loses its bond.

11
00:00:28.689 --> 00:00:31.089
A wallet with post-quantum signatures.

12
00:00:31.139 --> 00:00:34.339
A block explorer. Every job, in the open.

13
00:00:34.389 --> 00:00:37.139
A page where anyone can give the network a job.

14
00:00:37.189 --> 00:00:39.478
Now the network renders light,

15
00:00:40.939 --> 00:00:42.268
reads photos,

16
00:00:44.139 --> 00:00:46.139
writes a story, word by word,

17
00:00:46.189 --> 00:00:48.024
and checks every result.

18
00:00:48.927 --> 00:00:51.306
And this is just the beginning.

19
00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:55.071
Larger models. Longer context.

20
00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:57.599
Every one of them, verified.

21
00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:03.277
Many projects in this space are never independently audited.

22
00:01:03.327 --> 00:01:06.293
Vearl will be. Its code is already open.

23
00:01:06.343 --> 00:01:10.704
Not one more project. A foundation, built for the long run.

24
00:01:10.754 --> 00:01:14.685
An open network, for miners, developers, and partners.

25
00:01:14.735 --> 00:01:17.631
Proof of work, finally put to work.

26
00:01:18.085 --> 00:01:20.947
Public testnet. October 23.

